		<p id="drift-readout" class="chart-readout"></p>
		<div class="chart-panel">
			<div id="drift-chart" class="race-host" data-state="idle"></div>
			<div id="drift-legend" class="ring-legend"></div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>
<div id="seam-frame" class="chart-frame" hidden>
	<div class="chart-card chart-card--wide" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="seam-frame-title">
		<header class="chart-head">
			<div>
				<p class="chart-eyebrow">Satellites · within 100 miles</p>
				<h2 id="seam-frame-title">Fire history</h2>
			</div>
			<button type="button" id="seam-frame-close" class="chart-close" aria-label="Close">
				<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 4l8 8M12 4l-8 8"></path></svg>
			</button>
		</header>
		<p class="chart-help"><b>Why this matters:</b> in 2012 a sharper satellite camera (VIIRS) started watching for fires. It spots small fires the older cameras (MODIS) miss, so counts can jump after 2012 even if there weren't really more fires.</p>
		<p id="seam-readout" class="chart-readout"></p>
		<div class="seam-grid">
			<section class="chart-panel seam-panel">
				<p class="seam-cap">Fire days per year <span>each step up the side is 10× more, and the bars at the bottom show which satellites were watching</span></p>
				<div id="seam-chart" class="race-host" data-state="idle"></div>
				<div id="seam-legend" class="ring-legend"></div>
			</section>
			<section class="chart-panel seam-panel">
				<p class="seam-cap">Each week, before vs. after 2012 <span>dots above the dashed line got busier after 2012</span></p>
				<div id="seam-scatter" class="race-host" data-state="idle"></div>
				<div id="seam-scatter-legend" class="ring-legend"></div>
			</section>
		</div>
		<p class="seam-note">If both satellites saw the same fire on the same day, it is only counted once.</p>
	</div>
</div>
